/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) is entering a critical phase of maturity, marked by both unprecedented investment and unsustainable cost structures. While the global AI market is projected to exceed $1.8 trillion by 2030, the economics of AI remain fragile. Infrastructure expenditures, high energy consumption, and dependency on proprietary compute ecosystems have created a widening gap between technical progress and economic viability. For most startups and enterprises, scaling AI profitably in a short time span has become the core challenge.)
/E (Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) is entering a critical phase of maturity, marked by both unprecedented investment and unsustainable cost structures. While the global AI market is projected to exceed $1.8 trillion by 2030, the economics of AI remain fragile. Infrastructure expenditures, high energy consumption, and dependency on proprietary compute ecosystems have created a widening gap between technical progress and economic viability. For most startups and enterprises, scaling AI profitably in a short time span has become the core challenge.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
