317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The advent of Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) is fundamentally reshaping the global technological landscape, with the global AI market valued at approximately $391 billion in 2025 and projected to surpass $1.8 trillion by 2030 \(FF.co, 2025\). AI startups now account for over 6% of worldwide high-growth ventures and 9% of unicorns, reflecting intense investor interest, robust capital flows, and rapidly evolving innovation ecosystems \(CB Insights, 2025; Yahoo Finance, 2025\). However, beneath this optimistic surface lies a growing crisis of economic viability, especially concerning cost structure and profitability within the AI compute stack. Despite an influx of $44 billion in funding in the first half of 2025 \(Reuters, 2025; Ropes Gray, 2025\), the AI startup landscape is characterised by extreme volatility. Failure rates between 85% and 95% in the first five years are frequently reported, and fewer than 5% of companies reach sustainable scale \(MIT, 2025; Stanford HAI, 2025\). The harsh reality is that explosive investment does not guarantee commercial success. For every hundred AI startups founded, fewer than five achieve meaningful outcomes, while the vast majority succumb to insurmountable financial, technical, or strategic barriers.)
/E (The advent of Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) is fundamentally reshaping the global technological landscape, with the global AI market valued at approximately $391 billion in 2025 and projected to surpass $1.8 trillion by 2030 \(FF.co, 2025\). AI startups now account for over 6% of worldwide high-growth ventures and 9% of unicorns, reflecting intense investor interest, robust capital flows, and rapidly evolving innovation ecosystems \(CB Insights, 2025; Yahoo Finance, 2025\). However, beneath this optimistic surface lies a growing crisis of economic viability, especially concerning cost structure and profitability within the AI compute stack. Despite an influx of $44 billion in funding in the first half of 2025 \(Reuters, 2025; Ropes Gray, 2025\), the AI startup landscape is characterised by extreme volatility. Failure rates between 85% and 95% in the first five years are frequently reported, and fewer than 5% of companies reach sustainable scale \(MIT, 2025; Stanford HAI, 2025\). The harsh reality is that explosive investment does not guarantee commercial success. For every hundred AI startups founded, fewer than five achieve meaningful outcomes, while the vast majority succumb to insurmountable financial, technical, or strategic barriers.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
