322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (AI models, especially large language models \(LLMs\) and generative systems, demand enormous computational power for both training and inference. This translates to significant capital expenditure for specialised hardware \(e.g., GPUs\). Ongoing operations drive intensive operational expenditure due to power, cooling, data centre maintenance, and recurring cloud computing bills; these often reach millions of pounds per month for even mid-sized deployments \(TechWireAsia, 2025\). Expanding into new geographic regions further compounds these expenditures: higher import tariffs, unreliable energy grids, inefficient logistics, regulatory barriers, and local demand constraints greatly inflate total costs whilst purchasing power remains limited \(PACMI, 2025\).)
/E (AI models, especially large language models \(LLMs\) and generative systems, demand enormous computational power for both training and inference. This translates to significant capital expenditure for specialised hardware \(e.g., GPUs\). Ongoing operations drive intensive operational expenditure due to power, cooling, data centre maintenance, and recurring cloud computing bills; these often reach millions of pounds per month for even mid-sized deployments \(TechWireAsia, 2025\). Expanding into new geographic regions further compounds these expenditures: higher import tariffs, unreliable energy grids, inefficient logistics, regulatory barriers, and local demand constraints greatly inflate total costs whilst purchasing power remains limited \(PACMI, 2025\).)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
