/T (Hardware limitations force reliance on exclusive, vendor-controlled chips from a small group of dominant suppliers such as NVIDIA, Google, and AWS. These suppliers set premium prices, increasing costs for outsiders and restricting flexibility. Startups face high entry barriers and little leverage in negotiating access to cutting-edge compute resources \(Wired, 2025; TechWireAsia, 2025\).)
/E (Hardware limitations force reliance on exclusive, vendor-controlled chips from a small group of dominant suppliers such as NVIDIA, Google, and AWS. These suppliers set premium prices, increasing costs for outsiders and restricting flexibility. Startups face high entry barriers and little leverage in negotiating access to cutting-edge compute resources \(Wired, 2025; TechWireAsia, 2025\).)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
