/S /H2
/T (State-of-the-art models now measure from hundreds of millions to tens of billions of parameters. Such models simply do not fit on standard commodity servers. Specialised AI accelerators \(e.g., GPU\), high memory requirements, bandwidth, and power draw all contribute to high hosting expenses, especially for always-on, low-latency workloads \(TechWireAsia, 2025; arXiv INSIGHT, 2020\). Even deploying quantised or pruned versions leaves many opportunities for efficiency gains untapped, unless expertly engineered.)
/E (State-of-the-art models now measure from hundreds of millions to tens of billions of parameters. Such models simply do not fit on standard commodity servers. Specialised AI accelerators \(e.g., GPU\), high memory requirements, bandwidth, and power draw all contribute to high hosting expenses, especially for always-on, low-latency workloads \(TechWireAsia, 2025; arXiv INSIGHT, 2020\). Even deploying quantised or pruned versions leaves many opportunities for efficiency gains untapped, unless expertly engineered.)
