/T (Case studies demonstrate that inference costs for large models can be reduced by up to 99.7% through systematic optimization \(Databricks, 2023\). The Total Cost of Ownership \(TCO\) for a Frugal AI deployment using efficient hardware, open-source models, and edge-first strategies varies, with typical generative AI implementations for small- and medium-sized enterprises \(SMEs\) ranging from US $200,000 to US $500,000 over five years, and year-one costs of US $50,000 to US $100,000 \(Capgemini, 2024\). Ultra-lean deployments may achieve even lower TCOs.)
/E (Case studies demonstrate that inference costs for large models can be reduced by up to 99.7% through systematic optimization \(Databricks, 2023\). The Total Cost of Ownership \(TCO\) for a Frugal AI deployment using efficient hardware, open-source models, and edge-first strategies varies, with typical generative AI implementations for small- and medium-sized enterprises \(SMEs\) ranging from US $200,000 to US $500,000 over five years, and year-one costs of US $50,000 to US $100,000 \(Capgemini, 2024\). Ultra-lean deployments may achieve even lower TCOs.)
