/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Compute Layer The move to frugal, heterogeneous, and occasionally non-standard hardware increases the risk of physical security breaches, firmware exploits, and supply chain attacks. Academic studies raise concerns around insecure firmware, hardware Trojans, and networked device tampering, which could lead to widespread compromise. Security best practices include secure boot, hardware anti-tampering, supply chain audit, firmware patching, and root-of-trust protocols \(Digital AI, 2023; Securelist, 2025\).)
/E (Compute Layer The move to frugal, heterogeneous, and occasionally non-standard hardware increases the risk of physical security breaches, firmware exploits, and supply chain attacks. Academic studies raise concerns around insecure firmware, hardware Trojans, and networked device tampering, which could lead to widespread compromise. Security best practices include secure boot, hardware anti-tampering, supply chain audit, firmware patching, and root-of-trust protocols \(Digital AI, 2023; Securelist, 2025\).)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Orchestration Layer Edge-first orchestration and federated learning expose systems to new risks such as insecure communications, distributed denial-of-service, and malicious model poisoning. Every edge node, if unprotected, can serve as a conduit for data theft, model poisoning, or disruption of distributed operations. Encryption, authenticated aggregation, frequent software updates, and local monitoring are essential for network resilience \(Trend Micro, 2025; SUSE, 2025\).)
/E (Orchestration Layer Edge-first orchestration and federated learning expose systems to new risks such as insecure communications, distributed denial-of-service, and malicious model poisoning. Every edge node, if unprotected, can serve as a conduit for data theft, model poisoning, or disruption of distributed operations. Encryption, authenticated aggregation, frequent software updates, and local monitoring are essential for network resilience \(Trend Micro, 2025; SUSE, 2025\).)
