/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Open Foundation Open standards and APIs increase interoperability but also expand the attack surface through insecure plugins, vulnerable APIs, and improper privilege separation. Unprotected APIs or plugins can lead to remote code execution, data theft, and privilege escalation \(OWASP, 2024; Henrique, 2024\). Strong API authentication, privilege isolation, continuous security audits, and clear governance are industry best practices \(Trend Micro, 2025\).)
/E (Open Foundation Open standards and APIs increase interoperability but also expand the attack surface through insecure plugins, vulnerable APIs, and improper privilege separation. Unprotected APIs or plugins can lead to remote code execution, data theft, and privilege escalation \(OWASP, 2024; Henrique, 2024\). Strong API authentication, privilege isolation, continuous security audits, and clear governance are industry best practices \(Trend Micro, 2025\).)
