/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Trust, Governance, and Compliance Trust, transparency, and interpretability are critical for technical safety and regulatory compliance. Stakeholders demand clear decision pathways, accountability, and demonstrable system provenance. Academic work highlights the role of uncertainty-aware outputs, rigorous validation, and high standards of trust governance for the adoption and safety of AI systems \(Afroogh et al., 2024; KPMG, 2025\).)
