/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The long-term sustainability of Frugal AI is further underlined by its role in democratising innovation. By reducing energy and computing requirements, frugal approaches enable low-cost deployment in developing economies and resource-constrained public sectors, closing digital divides and promoting inclusive technological growth \(Frugal AI Hub, 2025; CSIS, 2025; EY, 2024\). Case studies from Kenya and Nigeria, for eg, demonstrate how localised public-private initiatives and modular, edge-first AI architectures are accelerating the digital inclusion and climate adaptation agenda, all while sharply lowering energy usage and emissions \(CSIS, 2025; TBI, 2025\).)
/E (The long-term sustainability of Frugal AI is further underlined by its role in democratising innovation. By reducing energy and computing requirements, frugal approaches enable low-cost deployment in developing economies and resource-constrained public sectors, closing digital divides and promoting inclusive technological growth \(Frugal AI Hub, 2025; CSIS, 2025; EY, 2024\). Case studies from Kenya and Nigeria, for eg, demonstrate how localised public-private initiatives and modular, edge-first AI architectures are accelerating the digital inclusion and climate adaptation agenda, all while sharply lowering energy usage and emissions \(CSIS, 2025; TBI, 2025\).)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [2]
>>
